    "text": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "topMargin": "5",
      "jcr:created": "Fri May 29 2026 19:21:55 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p>Arthritis is a widespread health challenge, serving as the leading cause of disability in the United States.<sup>1</sup> It’s a condition that affects nearly 60 million adults and children across the country.<sup>1</sup> This impact is only expected to grow, with projections suggesting that 78 million people will be living with the condition by 2040.<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>Despite its prevalence, arthritis is widely misunderstood. In this article, we're clearing up some misconceptions, because knowing the truth is the first step toward getting the right care. By clearing up common misunderstandings, more people may be able to find the path to effective care and essential medical technologies.</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jun 09 2026 20:06:59 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
