    "text_1963947648": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "jcr:created": "Fri May 29 2026 19:27:03 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Misconception</span>: Arthritis is a single disease.</h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">Reality</span></span></span><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">: Arthritis is an umbrella term for more than 100 conditions that affect the joints and surrounding tissue.<sup>2</sup></span></span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jun 02 2026 19:23:29 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "default": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "1",
          "width": "5"
        },
        "tablet": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "0",
          "width": "6"
        },
        "phone": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "offset": "0",
          "width": "12"
        }
      }
    },
    "text_458002293": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Fri May 29 2026 19:30:48 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>What they share are inflammation, pain and a progressive erosion of quality of life.</p>\n<p><b>Osteoarthritis (OA)</b> is the most common form, affecting an estimated 32.5 million U.S. adults. It's a degenerative condition driven by the breakdown of cartilage, the cushioning tissue that allows joints to move smoothly. As cartilage wears away, bone begins to rub against bone, causing pain, stiffness, swelling and eventually a significant loss of mobility. The hip and knee are among the joints most commonly and most severely affected.</p>\n<p><b>Rheumatoid arthritis (RA)</b> works differently. Rather than wear and tear, RA is an autoimmune disease. The body's immune system attacks the lining of the joints, causing inflammation that damages bone and cartilage over time.</p>\n<p><b>Post-traumatic arthritis</b>, a third common form, develops in a joint following an injury such as a fracture or ligament tear and can emerge years after the original trauma.</p>\n<p>All three conditions can progress to a point where they significantly impair the hip or knee and may ultimately require surgical intervention.</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri May 29 2026 19:32:27 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
